config-connector-extensions patch 0051: mockgcp answers a folder's or
organization's generateServiceIdentity with an operation already done.

The live run of serviceusage.gcp.hfl.dev ServiceIdentity on 2026-11-15
(run cce-11152217-c987, the test folder) found that the real API answers
services.generateServiceIdentity for folders/{id}/services/{service} with
an operation that is done, holds the identity, and is named
operations/finished.DONE_OPERATION; operations.get refuses that name
(400, "Invalid operation id"). Patch 0022's mock stored a normal
operation that a get could read, so the fake never showed it. Now
hierarchyidentity.go answers the same name, which no get finds. Applies
after 0022. Upstream candidate: with 0022.

diff --git a/mockgcp/mockserviceusage/hierarchyidentity.go b/mockgcp/mockserviceusage/hierarchyidentity.go
--- a/mockgcp/mockserviceusage/hierarchyidentity.go	2026-11-15 16:54:01
+++ b/mockgcp/mockserviceusage/hierarchyidentity.go	2026-11-15 16:54:01
@@ -32,6 +32,7 @@
 	"google.golang.org/genproto/googleapis/longrunning"
 	"google.golang.org/grpc/codes"
 	"google.golang.org/grpc/status"
+	"google.golang.org/protobuf/proto"
 	"google.golang.org/protobuf/types/known/anypb"
 )
 
@@ -71,5 +72,12 @@
 	if err := s.storage.Update(ctx, op.Name, op); err != nil {
 		return nil, true, err
 	}
-	return op, true, nil
+	// config-connector-extensions patch 0051: the real API answers a
+	// folder's or organization's generateServiceIdentity with an operation
+	// that is already done and named operations/finished.DONE_OPERATION,
+	// which operations.get refuses (400, "Invalid operation id"). Answer
+	// the same name; there is no stored operation by it, so a get fails.
+	done := proto.Clone(op).(*longrunning.Operation)
+	done.Name = "operations/finished.DONE_OPERATION"
+	return done, true, nil
 }
